<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bibliothèque nationale de France</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as National Library of France</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bibliothèque nationale de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> is the national library of France in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, which grew from the royal library of the French kings. It holds one of the world's largest collections of books, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>, maps, coins and prints. Among its treasures is the only surviving volume of the Korean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jikji">Jikji</a> of 1377, the oldest known book printed with movable metal type.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bibliotheque-nationale-de-france.jpg" alt="Bibliothèque nationale de France" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arthur Weidmann · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Biblioth%C3%A8que_Mitterrand_Mai_2022.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
